\"existing\"` disposition from `open()` is right once `#close` handles a closed owner.\n\nSecurity: F2 is an availability defect in the hosted OAuth layer manager. It grants no access and exposes no session. The head keeps a detached generation's rows, closing S1 F1. The other `HttpGeneration` transitions are unchanged. `disposed()` returns the existing `done` for a detached or abrupt state, and no `#close` path now calls `graceful()` on a detached generation.\n\nSimplification: no further change beyond F2. With the ternary, `#close` keeps one return path.\n\nThis verdict authorizes no deployment and closes no live acceptance.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3ae24db88f3a9cc2a7fd77c5b627b2553b11e87a","binding":"assigned","head":"ebd615fd99c766e356e87faa6b3b74098150a94f","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:efdba853ea0e506ea3513904cc4b491c84a4286e\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b9536c0f18bf3d7dca184079062b85804c23182e\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:4c2c799b5af3882c74f8705d20a5a28741a0e8ee\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b9536c0f18bf3d7dca184079062b85804c23182e","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}